{"step_index":1251,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T14:46:58Z","thinking":"**Verifying MAP Server Configuration**\n\nThe \"Connection test successful\" message confirms the MAP Engine server address is valid and reachable.  The displayed addresses for Legacy and \"Central\" differ in format, but the Engine server is working. The server address seen by \"Central\" doesn't specify a port.\n\n\n**Investigating HTTPS certificate issues**\n\nThe observed errors likely stem from an HTTPS certificate mismatch when connecting to `109.62.64.18:9443`. The browser's HTTPS request to the server with that address would fail due to certificate name mismatch, because the certificate is for `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` and not that IP.\nThe \"Connection test successful\" message is misleading because the test uses an HTTP request and therefore bypasses the certificate validation issue.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"/home/koby/.ansible/kssh 172.30.198.49 \"grep -rn 'Something went wrong' /usr/share/centreon/ 2>/dev/null || grep -rn 'server_address_ng' /usr/share/centreon/www/modules/centreon-map4-web-client/ 2>/dev/null\"","Cwd":"/home/koby","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Searching for Map monitoring code","toolSummary":"Grep for Map monitoring code"}}]}
